  "about": "Source rank rules (frameworks/knowledge/schemas/_system.md §4.1). A rule is a host plus a path prefix. The rule with the most path segments wins, then the one with more literal characters, then an exact host over a *. host. 'www.' is ignored, and hosts and paths compare in lower case. '*' in a prefix stands for one path segment. A URL no rule covers is tier B: the research worker rates it and the judge re-rates it. Add a rule only on V's yes.",
